    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 206.48,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "tokens left, we reject the request."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 209.04,
      "durationSeconds": 4,
      "text": "Let's see how this fixes our window"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 210.64,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "boundary problem. We set a bucket"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 213.04,
      "durationSeconds": 5.119,
      "text": "capacity of 100 tokens that refills at"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 215.84,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "100 tokens per minute. During quiet"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 218.159,
      "durationSeconds": 5.041,
      "text": "periods, tokens accumulate. When user"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 221.12,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "makes burst requests across window"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 223.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "boundaries, they consume accumulated"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 225.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "tokens but can't exceed the refill rate"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 227.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.639,
      "text": "over time. The key insight is that"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 229.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "tokens accumulate during quiet period."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 232.319,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "This allow legitimate traffic bursts"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 234.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "while maintaining the overall rate"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 236.159,
      "durationSeconds": 5.041,
      "text": "limit. A user can game the system by"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 238.64,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "timing the request to window boundaries."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 241.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "The algorithm uses two parameters."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 243.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Bucket capacity determines burst size"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 245.92,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "and refill rate determines sustained"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 247.92,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "throughput. A capacity of 100 with a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 250.64,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "refill rate of 100 per minute allows up"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 253.2,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "to 100 requests instantly that maintains"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 255.84,
      "durationSeconds": 4.239,
      "text": "exactly 100 requests per minute"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 257.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.799,
      "text": "long-term. There are other algorithms"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 260.079,
      "durationSeconds": 5.041,
      "text": "like sliding window logs, sliding window"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 262.479,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "counters, and leaking buckets that solve"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 265.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.68,
      "text": "the fixed window problem differently."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 267.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.521,
      "text": "But token buckets strike the best"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 268.8,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "balance between simplicity and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 270.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "effectiveness for most use cases. Now"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 273.44,
      "durationSeconds": 3.759,
      "text": "that we have our algorithm, we need to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 275.36,
      "durationSeconds": 3.92,
      "text": "decide where to implement it in our"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 277.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.761,
      "text": "system architecture. We have three"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 279.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.08,
      "text": "options for where to place our ray"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 280.96,
      "durationSeconds": 4.959,
      "text": "limiter. Client side ray limiting puts"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 283.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "the logic in client applications, but we"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 285.919,
      "durationSeconds": 4.401,
      "text": "can't trust clients to enforce their own"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 287.68,
      "durationSeconds": 5.76,
      "text": "limits. Malicious users can modify the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 290.32,
      "durationSeconds": 5.599,
      "text": "code or bypass restrictions entirely."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 293.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Serverside ray limiting embeds the logic"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 295.919,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "in our application code. This gives us"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 298.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.239,
      "text": "complete control over the algorithm and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 300.479,
      "durationSeconds": 3.841,
      "text": "keeps everything in one place. The"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 302.479,
      "durationSeconds": 3.841,
      "text": "downsides is that ray limiting gets"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 304.32,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "mixed with business logic and each"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 306.32,
      "durationSeconds": 4.879,
      "text": "service needs its own implementation."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 308.88,
      "durationSeconds": 5.039,
      "text": "Middleware ray limiting uses a dedicated"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 311.199,
      "durationSeconds": 5.201,
      "text": "service between clients and the APIs."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 313.919,
      "durationSeconds": 5.28,
      "text": "This could be an API gateway, a reverse"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 316.4,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "proxy or a custom service. This keeps"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 319.199,
      "durationSeconds": 4.081,
      "text": "ray limiting separate from business"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 320.96,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "logic and provides a single place to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 323.28,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "manage policies. The trade-off is an"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 325.68,
      "durationSeconds": 4.32,
      "text": "increase in system complexity. Which"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 328.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "should we choose? It depends on our"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 330,
      "durationSeconds": 4.96,
      "text": "situation. If we already have an API"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 332.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "gateway handling authentication, adding"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 334.96,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "rate limiting there makes sense. If we"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 337.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "need a custom algorithm, server side"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 339.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "gives us flexibility. For most systems,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 342.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "middleware offers the best balance of"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 344.08,
      "durationSeconds": 5.119,
      "text": "control and operational simplicity. Our"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 347.12,
      "durationSeconds": 3.84,
      "text": "system architecture looks like this. We"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 349.199,
      "durationSeconds": 3.921,
      "text": "store ray limiting rules in a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 350.96,
      "durationSeconds": 5.2,
      "text": "configuration service. These rules"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 353.12,
      "durationSeconds": 5.44,
      "text": "define limits like premium users get a"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 356.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "th00and requests per hour or free users"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 358.56,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "get 100 requests per hour. The"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 360.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "middleware fetches these rules and"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 362.32,
      "durationSeconds": 4.719,
      "text": "stores token bucket state in Reddus."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 364.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.479,
      "text": "When a request arrives, the middleware"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 367.039,
      "durationSeconds": 4.401,
