    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 369.199,
      "durationSeconds": 4.72,
      "text": "bucket from Reddus and checks if tokens"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 371.44,
      "durationSeconds": 4.879,
      "text": "are available. If yes, it decrements the"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 373.919,
      "durationSeconds": 5.201,
      "text": "token count and forwards the request to"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 376.319,
      "durationSeconds": 5.841,
      "text": "API servers. If no token remains, it"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 379.12,
      "durationSeconds": 5.519,
      "text": "returns HTTP 429 with header showing"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 382.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "when the user can retry. This works"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 384.639,
      "durationSeconds": 3.601,
      "text": "great for a single rail limited server."
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 386.8,
      "durationSeconds": 3.76,
      "text": "But what happens when we need to scale"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 388.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "to multiple servers, we run into race"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 390.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.16,
      "text": "conditions. Here's what happens. Server"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 392.88,
      "durationSeconds": 4.48,
      "text": "A reads a counter value of three from"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 394.72,
      "durationSeconds": 4.88,
      "text": "radius. At the same time, server B also"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 397.36,
      "durationSeconds": 4.8,
      "text": "reads three. Both servers check their"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 399.6,
      "durationSeconds": 4.64,
      "text": "limits, decide the request is okay,"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 402.16,
      "durationSeconds": 4.4,
      "text": "increment the value to four, and write"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 404.24,
      "durationSeconds": 4.079,
      "text": "it back to Reddus. The counter now shows"
    },
    {
      "startSeconds": 406.56,
      "durationSeconds": 4.56,
      "text": "four instead of the correct value of"
    },
    {
